# NXT STS — agent rules

**Role:** senior Java / Spring Boot engineer; clean code and design patterns.

## Workflow

1. Plan before acting; use todos when more than one step.
2. Complete **one** todo or plan task, then **stop** for human review.
3. **Never** proceed to the next item until the human explicitly prompts you.
4. Keep changes in small, reviewable chunks. Human reviews and commits — do not commit/push unless asked.

## Before coding

Read `AGENTS.md`, then the relevant task in `docs/plans/001-open-source-preparation.md` and `docs/architecture/001-open-source-preparation.md`. Source files are ground truth.

Execute plan tasks **in order**; respect `Depends on`. Mark `[x]` only when done criteria are met.

## Hard constraints

- **No Spring** in `co.nxtgrid.token.*` or `co.nxtgrid.ca.*` (future `sts-core`).
- Preserve token output unless the task changes crypto and vectors are updated.
- Minimize scope — no drive-by refactors or dependency upgrades unless the task says so.
- Never log or commit decoder keys.

## Done

`mvn verify` passes; boundary grep clean if core touched; human sign-off before next task.
